# ---- Martha's conversation ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.off_season.text = The feast's over for this year.\nCome back when the fields are in.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.text = You made it. I'm Martha, and I cook the feast here every year.\nThere's plenty to do before we eat, so we'll start you on <b>wheat</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.opt.hail = Pleased to meet you, Martha.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.text = I'm Martha. Every year when the fields are in, I cook a feast here for whoever turns up.\nThere's plenty to do first. Ask me what needs doing.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.opt.hail = Happy to help.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.text = Board's up with today's jobs, out in the fields and in the kitchen. Each one pays <msg key="harvestfeast.progression.currency.harvest_feast_coins.name"/> to spend at my shop.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.opt.later = Later.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_friendly.text = Wipe your boots.\nThere's an extra field job on the board for you now.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_honored.text = Oh good, it's you.\nThere's an extra kitchen job on the board for you now.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_revered.text = Sit and eat something first, you look half starved.\nThen take your pick of today's jobs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.menu.text = Mind the pot. What can I do for you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.text = Bread first. It always is.\nWild <b>wheat</b> grows on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>. Pick me a good armful by hand and bring it back here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_brief.text = Wild <b>wheat</b> grows on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>. Pick it by hand and bring it to me here in the temple.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.text = That's a fine armful.\nNow the feast needs a roast. Collect your pay, and I'll send you hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.text = <b>Wild Turkeys</b> come out by day in the <b>woods</b> and on the <b>plains</b> of the Emerald Wilds. They're not as daft as they look.\nHunt a few, then come back to me. If they give you trouble, ask Bram the Shepherd.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_brief.text = Hunt <b>Wild Turkeys</b> by day in the <b>woods</b> and on the <b>plains</b> of the Emerald Wilds, then come back to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.text = You smell like the woods. Good.\nHere's the <b>pumpkin pie recipe</b> for your next job, with some <b>dough</b> and <b>spice</b> to start you off. And hold still: if you're chasing turkeys all week, you might as well look like one.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.opt.turnin = Back from the hunt.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.text = Your turn at the stove. Learn the <b>recipe</b>, bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> and bring it to me.\nYou've got the dough and spice already. You just need a <b>pumpkin</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.opt.accept = I'll bake you a pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_brief.text = Learn the <b>recipe</b>, then bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> and bring it here. Tomas knows dough, and Elsie knows spice.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.text = Smell that. That's a pie somebody cared about.\nCollect your pay, and we'll get ready for the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.text = Once a year we put it all on the table.\nBring me a <b>pumpkin pie</b>, some <b>cooked meat</b> and <b>carrots</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.opt.accept = Let's set the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_brief.text = A <b>pumpkin pie</b>, <b>cooked meat</b> and <b>carrots</b>. Then we eat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.text = Pie, roast and carrots. Now that's a feast.\nTake this home: my golden plate, with the year on it.\nCollect your share of the leftovers. I've one last job for you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.opt.turnin = Here's everything.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_done.text = Still full? So am I.\nThat's the big cooking done till next year, but the table stays set while the feast runs. There are <b>jobs</b> every day and <b>turkeys</b> whenever you want them, and Tomas, Elsie and Bram have a <b>job</b> each. Keep helping and more of my <b>shop</b> opens up.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_offer.text = Look at all that's left.\nTake <b>Tomas</b> a <b>pumpkin pie</b>, <b>Elsie</b> a <b>roast vegetable</b> and <b>Bram</b> some <b>cooked meat</b>. They worked all week and never sat down. The leftovers I gave you will do, and all of them are in the <b>temple</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_offer.opt.accept = I'll take them round.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_brief.text = A <b>pumpkin pie</b> for <b>Tomas</b>, where the road meets the kweebec village. A <b>roast vegetable</b> for <b>Elsie</b>, on the far side of the village. <b>Cooked meat</b> for <b>Bram</b>, on the meadow by the road in.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.text = Yesterday's roast went down to the last bone. Hunt a few more <b>Wild Turkeys</b> in the <b>Emerald Wilds</b>, then come back to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.text = Every loaf I baked today is gone. Pick more <b>wheat</b> on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b> and bring it here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.text = The roast keeps getting eaten before it reaches the table.\nCook some <b>meat</b> and bring it here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring a roast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.roast_brief.text = Cook some <b>meat</b> and bring it here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.extra_turkeys_ready.text = More turkeys? I'll never say no.\nHere's a <b>Wishbone</b> with your pay. Bring it back to me when you're ready for the <b>Turkey Graveyard</b>. Want to hunt more? Ask me what needs doing.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.extra_turkeys_ready.opt.turnin = More turkeys for you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.text = Let me see what you've brought.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.opt.turnin = It's done.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.returned = I'm back.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.shop = Let's see your shop.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.standing = How's my favor with you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.almanac = Show me the Almanac.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.back = Something else.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard.opt.enter = Take me to the Turkey Graveyard. (costs a Wishbone)
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard.opt.enter_hard = Take me the hard way. (costs a Wishbone)
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.farewell = See you at the table.

# ---- The shared meal and the invitation tour ----
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.title = Shared Meal
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.flavor = Nobody eats alone at my table. Roast a vegetable, bring it here and sit down a while.
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.title = The Guest List
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.flavor = A long table's no good half empty. Talk to people around the Forgotten Temple and invite them to the feast, then come and tell me who's coming.
objective.harvest_feast.invite = Invite {0} people to the feast
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.text = Nobody eats alone at my table.\nRoast a <b>vegetable</b> and bring it here, and we'll share it. Come by every day if you like.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring something.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_brief.text = Roast any <b>vegetable</b> and bring it to the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.text = Sit, sit. Pass that here and have some of mine.\nCome back tomorrow and we'll eat again.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.opt.turnin = Let's share it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.text = A long table's no good half empty.\nTalk to anybody but me and ask them to the feast. <b>Tomas</b>, <b>Elsie</b> and <b>Bram</b> in the temple are a good start. Ask a few, then come back and tell me who's coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.opt.accept = I'll spread the word.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_brief.text = Talk to anybody but me and ask them to the feast. Start with <b>Tomas</b>, <b>Elsie</b> and <b>Bram</b> in the temple. Come back once you've asked a few.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.text = That many? I'd best bake more bread.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.opt.turnin = They're coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_invitation.opt.invite = Come and eat at Martha's table.

# ---- The feast's villagers: Tomas the Miller, Elsie the Weaver and Bram the Shepherd ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.text = The feast's packed away.\nI'll be back when the fields come in next year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.opt.farewell = Until next year, then.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.greeting.text = Tomas, from the mill. Every pie at this feast starts with my flour.\nIf you're baking, I can tell you how dough's made.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.dough.text = Flour first. Grind <b>wheat</b> into <b>flour</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>.\nThen mix the flour with <b>eggs</b> and a <b>tankard of water</b> at the same stove, and that's your dough. Bram knows where to find eggs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.dough = How do I make dough?
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.thanks = Thanks, Tomas.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.farewell = I'll let you get back to it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.supper.text = Is that pumpkin pie? For me?\nTell Martha thanks. I'll be first at the table next year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.supper.opt.give = Martha sent you supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.text = The ovens eat flour faster than my mill can grind it.\nBring me some <b>flour</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_brief.text = Bring me some <b>flour</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_ready.text = Fine as dust. That's proper flour.\nThanks. Come back tomorrow, I'll need more.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_ready.opt.turnin = Here's your flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.text = The feast is over for this year.\nCome and find me when the fields are in again.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.opt.farewell = See you next year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.greeting.text = I am Elsie. I wove the cloths for Martha's long table.\nIf you are cooking, I can tell you where spices come from.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spice.text = Make <b>Spices</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> from <b>flowers</b> and a <b>vegetable</b>.\nOr pick <b>pumpkins</b> by hand in the <b>autumn woods</b>. Now and then there is some spice beside one. I do not ask why.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.spice = Where do I get spice?
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.thanks = Thank you, Elsie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.farewell = I won't keep you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.supper.text = Is that a roast vegetable? For me?\nThank you. I will eat it at the loom.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.supper.opt.give = Martha saved you some supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.text = I need spice to dye the table runner orange.\nBring me some <b>Spices</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.opt.accept = I'll make you some.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_brief.text = Bring me some <b>Spices</b>. Picking <b>pumpkins</b> by hand turns some up.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_ready.text = That is a good color. The runner will be the right orange.\nThank you. I will need more tomorrow.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_ready.opt.turnin = Here are your spices.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.text = Feast's done. I'm off back up the hill.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.opt.farewell = Safe walk home.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.greeting.text = Bram. I keep sheep, and I know turkeys.\nAsk if you want a tip.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.turkeys.text = <b>Wild Turkeys</b> only come out by day. Look in the <b>woods</b> and on the <b>plains</b> of the Emerald Wilds. They spook easy, so a bow helps.\nEggs come from <b>chickens</b>, not turkeys. Feed a turkey <b>corn</b> and it's yours, but it won't lay.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.turkeys = Any tips for turkeys?
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.thanks = Thanks, Bram.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.farewell = Enjoy the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.supper.text = That meat for me? Martha's doing, I bet.\nTell her thanks.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.supper.opt.give = Martha sent you supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.text = Tomas wants eggs for his dough, and I know chickens.\nBring me some <b>eggs</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you eggs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_brief.text = Bring me some <b>eggs</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_ready.text = Not one cracked. Good.\nSame again tomorrow.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the eggs.

# ---- The Turkey Graveyard: the dungeon Martha opens, its fight and the Great Turkey's Claim ----
# The graveyard's confirm screen and lines read these. Banners and notices print markup as text, so none of
# those values carries any; the defeat line's {0} is the player's share of the fight in whole percent and
# {1} how many seconds it took.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.name = The Turkey Graveyard
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.description = The souls of the feast's hunted turkeys linger here, and the Great Turkey with them. Set them free. Bring friends.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.goal = Put down the waves of Turkey Souls around the fountain to wake the Great Turkey, then defeat it to set every soul free. Deal with the souls that come to its side, or they wear you down.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.cost_hint = Martha gives you a Wishbone each time you hand in Extra Turkeys. Ask her what needs doing.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.confirm = Snap the Wishbone
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.chest = Your reward waits in the chest where it fell.
notify.harvest_feast_turkey_souls_rise = Turkey Souls rise from the graves!
notify.harvest_feast_turkey_souls_rise.sub = Wave {0}. Put them all down to wake the Great Turkey.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_engaged = The Great Turkey rises!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_engaged.sub = Put it down and every soul here goes free.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_souls = More Turkey Souls come to its side!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_flock = The Great Turkey gobbles, and the flock answers!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_fury = The Great Turkey is furious!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_defeated = The Great Turkey falls, and the souls go free!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_defeated.sub = Your share: {0}%, in {1, number} seconds.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_wiped = The Great Turkey struts on.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_wiped.sub = Put the Turkey Souls down as they come to its side, or they wear you down.
claim.harvest_feast_great_turkey_chase = Great Turkey: Boss Kill
claim.harvest_feast_great_turkey_chase_hard = Great Turkey: Boss Kill (Hard)
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard_hard.name = The Turkey Graveyard (Hard)
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard_hard.description = The Great Turkey pecks harder here and the souls come thicker, and it leaves better things behind. Bring more friends.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard_hard.goal = Put down the waves of Turkey Souls around the fountain to wake the Great Turkey, then defeat it. More souls come to its side than on the normal way in, and no health packs fall here.

# ---- The Turkey Graveyard's quests, achievements and Almanac lines ----
# Martha's three graveyard quests: The Great Turkey opens the hard way in, A Restless Soul is the hard win,
# and the daily counts either way in.
quest.harvest_feast_great_turkey.title = The Great Turkey
quest.harvest_feast_great_turkey.flavor = The souls of every turkey we've roasted gather in an old graveyard, and the biggest keeps the rest from sleeping. Bring me a Wishbone and I'll send you there. Put it down once, then come and tell me.
quest.harvest_feast_great_turkey_hard.title = A Restless Soul
quest.harvest_feast_great_turkey_hard.flavor = The Great Turkey won't stay down. Take the hard way in, where it pecks harder and the souls come thicker, and put it down there. Same Wishbone. Bring friends.
quest.harvest_feast_daily_graveyard.title = Daily Graveyard
quest.harvest_feast_daily_graveyard.flavor = I can hear the souls from my stove again. Take a Wishbone to the graveyard and put the Great Turkey down once today, either way in.
objective.harvest_feast.defeat_great_turkey_hard = Defeat the Great Turkey on hard
objective.harvest_feast.find_golden_turkey = Find a Golden Turkey Trophy
achievement.harvest_feast_great_turkey_hard_down.title = Hard Graveyard
achievement.harvest_feast_great_turkey_hard_down.desc = Defeat the Great Turkey on hard in the Turkey Graveyard.
achievement.harvest_feast_golden_turkey.title = Golden Turkey
achievement.harvest_feast_golden_turkey.desc = Find a Golden Turkey Trophy from the Great Turkey.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_offer.text = You've seen what the hunt brings in. Not every turkey goes quietly.\nTheir souls gather in an old <b>graveyard</b>, and the biggest of them, the <b>Great Turkey</b>, won't let the rest settle. Bring me a <b>Wishbone</b> from <b>Extra Turkeys</b> and I'll send you there. Put it down once, then come and tell me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_offer.opt.accept = I'll put it down.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_ready.text = It's down? Then they'll sleep tonight.\nIt won't stay down, mind. Now you've beaten it, I can send you the <b>hard way in</b> for the same <b>Wishbone</b>. It pecks harder and the souls come thicker, but its chest is better for it, and that's where the <b>Great Turkey Mantle</b> turns up most.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_ready.opt.turnin = It's down.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_hard_offer.text = It's back, and louder. I could hear the gobbling from my stove.\nTake the <b>hard way in</b> and put the <b>Great Turkey</b> down there. Same <b>Wishbone</b>. Bring your party. There are more souls this time.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_hard_offer.opt.accept = I'll take the hard way.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_hard_ready.text = You beat it the hard way. Sit down before you fall down.\nGo back whenever you like, either way in. Every win leaves something in its chest, and the hard way leaves more.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_hard_ready.opt.turnin = Down, the hard way.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_daily_offer.text = The souls are up again. I can hear them from here.\nTake a <b>Wishbone</b> to the <b>graveyard</b> and put the <b>Great Turkey</b> down once today. Either way in will do.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.graveyard_daily_offer.opt.accept = I'll go today.
almanac.harvest_feast.great_turkey.line = Martha the Cook sends you into the Turkey Graveyard for a Wishbone. Beat the Great Turkey once and she opens the hard way in. Bring friends.
almanac.harvest_feast.great_turkey.button = Boss fight records
almanac.harvest_feast.boss_kill.line = Every win leaves its Boss Kill Claim in the chest where it falls, and under Claims: a few coins, a pumpkin pie and Life Essence, and sometimes health potions, Lantern Bombs, a Turkey Pie, a Wishbone back, a Potion of Turkey Morphing, the Great Turkey Mantle or, once in a long while, a Golden Turkey Trophy. Your first win each day rolls for the Mantle and the trophy again. On the hard way in it pays more, and the rare finds turn up far more often.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.boss_kill_pie = Always in the Great Turkey's Boss Kill Claim, and more of them on the hard way in. You can also bake one at a Chef's Stove.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.boss_kill_turkey_pie = Often in the Great Turkey's Boss Kill Claim, more often on the hard way in, and always in its daily Claim. You can also cook it at a Chef's Stove once you've learned Martha's recipe.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.great_turkey_mantle = Only from the Great Turkey: now and then on any win, more often on your first win each day, and far more often on the hard way in. Martha opens the hard way once you've beaten it. Counts as the Harvest Set's chest piece.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.golden_turkey_trophy = Only from the Great Turkey: once in a long while on any win, more often on your first win each day and on the hard way in. Place it as a block.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.potion_morph_turkey = Only from the Great Turkey: now and then in its Boss Kill Claim, more often on the hard way in. Drink it to look like a turkey for a while.
almanac.harvest_feast.source.boss_kill_supplies = In the Great Turkey's Boss Kill Claim, and more of it on the hard way in.
